# Git hooks must stay LF — a CRLF shebang (`#!/bin/sh\r`) breaks the hook under
# any non-git-for-Windows `sh`/dash. Pin the shipped pre-commit hooks to LF so a
# Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true can't rewrite them. (STORY-01.5.03 review.)
_00-Project-Management/93-Scripts/hooks/pre-commit text eol=lf

# The plugin-metrics time series is appended from a Windows dev machine and from
# the Linux CI runner. Pin to LF so each daily commit is a one-line diff rather
# than a whole-file EOL rewrite, which would bury the actual change.
data/plugin-metrics/*.csv  text eol=lf
data/plugin-metrics/*.json text eol=lf

# The retro-ledger test fixtures encode their LINE ENDINGS as part of the fixture.
# The live ledger is CRLF in a working tree and LF in git; an LF-only fixture never
# exercises the CRLF arm of the reader, and last phase exactly that let a mutant pass
# 44 green checks while the live derivation returned 1 story for a month that had 39
# (BUG-20260804-17). `-text` disables ALL eol conversion so the committed bytes — a
# deliberate CRLF/LF mix — survive a fresh clone unchanged. Do not "tidy" this to
# `text eol=lf`; `tests/retro-report.test.js :: all-levels` asserts the mix is still
# there and will fail loudly if it is normalised away.
_00-Project-Management/93-Scripts/tests/fixtures/retro/*.jsonl -text

# Same reasoning as the retro fixtures above, for the FEAT-26.4 autopilot fixtures: the
# run/pause ledger fixture is a deliberate CRLF/LF MIX so the reader's CRLF arm is actually
# exercised. `-text` disables all eol conversion so the committed bytes survive a fresh
# clone. `tests/autopilot-run-plan.test.js` and `tests/plan-vs-actual.test.js` assert the
# mix is still there.
_00-Project-Management/93-Scripts/tests/fixtures/autopilot/*.jsonl -text

# The thin-corpus fixture (STORY-28.1.04) is LF in this working tree with no attribute, so on
# a fresh clone with core.autocrlf=true it would arrive CRLF and the bytes under test would
# differ between machines — a fixture whose content is a claim about MEASUREMENT must not vary
# by checkout (review MINOR-7). `-text` disables all eol conversion, same reasoning as the two
# fixture sets above.
_00-Project-Management/93-Scripts/tests/fixtures/thin-corpus/** -text
